{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaSignThreshold"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.y_pos_of_no_deep_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.y_pos_of_no_deep_cells","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaNormalizationSign.lean#L126-L138","doc":"**No deep cells ⇒ `y_λ > 0`**, unconditionally.  At `q₀` a below-threshold cell needs\ncontent `≤ −3`, hence `≥ 4` rows — so every `λ` with `ℓ(λ) ≤ 3` carries a *strictly positive*\nWedderburn weight.  `(8,1)` is the case that refutes the naive `ℓ`-parity reading. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.y_sign_of_closedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.y_sign_of_closedForm","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaNormalizationSign.lean#L97-L124","doc":"**`sign(y_λ) = (−1)^{P(λ)}`, with no residual global sign.**\n\nGiven `Z` in closed form (the classical `Σ f^λ s_λ = p₁ⁿ`, supplied as `hZ`), dividing the\nWenzl weight by `Z` preserves sign, so the content-threshold parity of\n`YLambdaSignThreshold.wenzl_sign` transfers verbatim from `s_λ` to `y_λ`.\n\nThis is the statement #4662 could not make: there, `sign(Z)` was verified numerically for\n`n = 2..12` but underived, so the parity determined `sign(y_λ)` only up to one global sign per\n`n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.normalization_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.normalization_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaNormalizationSign.lean#L90-L93","doc":"**`Z ≠ 0`** — the form needed to divide by it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.normalization_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.normalization_pos","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaNormalizationSign.lean#L81-L88","doc":"**`Z > 0` for every `n`.**  A positive base raised to a natural power.\n\nWorth stating explicitly that this is *not* inherited from the summands: `Z = Σ_λ f^λ s_λ` has\nmixed-sign terms — that is precisely `YLambdaSignThreshold.wenzl_sign` — so term-by-term\npositivity is false.  The closed form is what forces the sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.base_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.base_pos","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaNormalizationSign.lean#L75-L79","doc":"**The base is positive.**  In the substrate regime `Q > 1` and `Qʳ > 1`, so `1 − Qʳ < 0`\nand `1 − Q < 0`: the ratio of two negatives.  This is the whole mechanism — the positivity of\n`Z` comes from a *cancellation of two sign flips*, not from any term being positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.normalizationClosedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.YLambdaNormalizationSign.normalizationClosedForm","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/YLambdaNormalizationSign.lean#L70-L73","doc":"The closed form for the Wenzl normalisation: `Z = ((1 − Qʳ)/(1 − Q))ⁿ`, the `n`-th power of\nthe principal specialisation of the first power sum `p₁ = 1 + Q + ⋯ + Q^{r−1}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}